{
  "analysis": "I now have enough information to write the MIPS interpreter. The ELF is 32-bit little-endian MIPS32r2, entry 0x400110, with segments at 0x400000 and 0x466520, huge BSS (~1GB). The custom stdlib uses nonstandard syscall numbers (read=0, write=1, open=2, close=3, lseek=8, exit=60, etc.) and frames are saved as /tmp/frame.bmp every 10th DG_DrawFrame call. I need to check the O_* flags and WAD search paths, then write vm.js.",
  "plan": "Check O_* constants in my_stdlib.h and WAD search paths in d_iwad.c. Then write a comprehensive vm.js MIPS32r2 interpreter with sparse memory, delay slots, FPU, and host file I/O syscalls.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -nE \"#define O_|USE_FS|doomgeneric_Create|D_DoomMain|iwad|IWAD|wad\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.h /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/d_iwad.c /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric.c 2>/dev/null | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,280p' /tmp/stdlib_lines.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
